  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0c5cbb483bddf4c478998c8960188805, type: 3}
  m_Name: L5_ShadowBadEndIntro
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueData
  Lines:
  - (His voice softens, losing its edge. It sounds relieved, almost like a tired
    sigh.)
  - Good choice. Why run when you can finally rest?
  - "Look at the sun. It\u2019s perfect right there, isn't it? Just an inch above
    the horizon. If we don\u2019t move, it never has to set. If we don\u2019t move,
    she never has to leave."
  - "Sit down, Minh. Put the camera away. You don\u2019t need to capture anything
    else, because nothing after this moment is worth remembering."
  - Let the world outside move on. Let them go to school, let them work, let them
    grow old and forget.
  - "We\u2019ll stay here in the golden hour, where the tea is still warm and her
    hand is still on your shoulder."
  - "Close your eyes. No more 'clicks.' No more 'flashes.' Just... silence. We\u2019re
    finally a finished photograph..."
  - ... And photographs never have to say goodbye.
